    "pdpPlainTextPreview": "The Sovereign 1995 is a piece of historical interest and is struck to proof standard, containing the third portrait of Her Majesty by Raphael Maklouf.\nWE ARE STRENGTHENING ACCOUNT SECURITY AND PROTECTING YOUR ACCESS WITH 2 STEP VERIFICATION. FIND OUT MORE Home Sovereign All Sovereign Coins The Sovereign 1995 Share via Gold Proof The Sovereign 1995 Proof Price: £1,380.00 Add to basket Quantity ADD TO BASKET Limited Stock | 1 - 10 working days for orders to the UK PRODUCT CODE: HISSOV95 Contains the third portrait of Her Late Majesty by Raphael Maklouf Proof quality Gold Proof Read the full description YOU MIGHT ALSO BE INTERESTED IN ADD TO BASKET Britannia 2026 1oz Silver Bullion Coin £62.49 In Stock ADD TO BASKET Britannia 2022 1 oz Silver Bullion Coin £61.29 In Stock ADD TO BASKET Level 5 Genius Medal £9.95 In Stock ADD TO BASKET Britannia 2026 1oz Gold Bullion Coin £3,485.74 In Stock ADD TO BASKET 100th Anniversary of the Birth of Queen Elizabeth II 2026 UK £5 Brilliant Uncirculated Coin £17.50 In Stock ADD TO BASKET Britannia 2026 1oz Silver Bullion Twenty-Five Coin Tube £1,482.25 In Stock ADD TO BASKET Level 4 Mastermind Medal £9.95 In Stock ADD TO BASKET Britannia 1g Gold Bullion Minted Bar £140.73 In Stock ADD TO BASKET Level 3 Decoder Medal £9.95 In Stock ADD TO BASKET Level 2 Explorer Medal and Collector Folder £9.95 In Stock From 1985 to 1997, UK circulating coins featured a royal portrait by the sculptor Raphael Maklouf. The portrait was couped and showed The Queen wearing the royal diadem, which she normally wears on her way to and from the State Opening of Parliament. Unlike the earlier portraits, Maklouf’s version also shows The Queen wearing a necklace and earrings. Critics accused him of sculpting The Queen “flatteringly young” but Maklouf responded by pointing out that his intention had been “to create a symbol, regal and ageless.” If you look closely you can see the artist’s initials, ‘RDM’, at the bottom of The Queen’s neck. Maklouf included his middle initial, D for David, to make sure that his initials wouldn’t be seen as a reference to The Royal Mint. SPECIFICATION The Sovereign 1995 proof Specification Value Denomination Sovereign Alloy 22 Carat Gold Weight 7.98 g Diameter 22.05mm Reverse Designer Benedetto Pistrucci Specification Value Obverse Designer Raphael Maklouf Quality Proof Year 1995 Pure Metal Type Gold"
